    "gradeBand": "7",
    "overview": "Judge samples, make estimates and compare two groups with data.",
    "problems": [
      {
        "prompt": "A principal wants to know how all 900 students feel about a new schedule. Which sample is best: the 15 students on the basketball team, the first 30 students who arrive in the morning, or 90 students chosen at random from the school roster? Explain."
      },
      {
        "prompt": "In the random sample of 90 students, 54 like the new schedule. Estimate how many of the 900 students like it."
      },
      {
        "prompt": "Quiz scores: Class 1: 6, 7, 7, 8, 9, 11. Class 2: 8, 9, 10, 10, 11, 12. Find the mean and the mean absolute deviation of each class. Round to the nearest hundredth."
      },
      {
        "prompt": "Use your answers to problem 3. How many MADs apart are the means (use the larger MAD)? Which class typically scored higher, and how much do the two distributions overlap?"
      },
      {
        "prompt": "Two random samples of 10 seventh graders were asked whether they have a pet. In one sample, 40% said yes; in the other, 70% said yes. Why can two random samples give such different results, and what could you do to get a better estimate?"
      }
    ],
